  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe proposed strategy leverages a multi-scale optimization approach combined with simulated annealing to escape local minima and explore the solution space efficiently. By starting with coarse discretizations and gradually increasing resolution, the method ensures computational efficiency while maintaining feasibility through precise repair mechanisms. The key innovation lies in systematically balancing exploration and exploitation across different scales, allowing for the discovery of high-quality solutions without being trapped by local optima.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Representation: h \u2208 [0,1]^{n_points}, \u2211h_i = n_points / 2.\n- Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k (h * (1 - h))[k] * dx, computed via FFT-based convolution.\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1, \u2211h_i dx = 1.\n- Annealing schedule: Temperature T(t) decreases exponentially with time steps.\n- Multi-scale: Start with low n_points (e.g., 20), double resolution every 500 steps.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nA. Initialization\n1. Use initial_h_values if provided.\n2. Downsample to 20 points: h_low = interpolate(initial_h, 20).\n3. Set n_points = 20, best_h = h_low, C\u2085_best = evaluate(h_low).\n\nB. Simulated Annealing Loop\n1. For each temperature iteration:\n   a. Perturb h by adding Gaussian noise scaled by current temperature.\n   b. Repair h: clip to [0,1], rescale sum to n_points / 2.\n   c. Compute C\u2085_new.\n   d. Accept perturbation if C\u2085_new < C\u2085_best or with probability exp((C\u2085_current - C\u2085_new)/T).\n2. Every 500 steps, double n_points and interpolate best_h to new grid.\n3. After each resolution change, re-optimize using gradient descent.\n4. Maintain global best at each scale.\n\nC. Gradient Descent Refinement\n1. Compute gradient of C\u2085 with respect to h using finite differences.\n2. Update h: h = h - lr * gradient.\n3. Repair h to satisfy constraints.\n\nD. Termination\n1. Stop after budget_s seconds or when T < 1e-6.\n2. Ensure final h satisfies constraints and recompute C\u2085.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Default: Starting n_points=20, doubling up to 200.\n- Annealing schedule: T0=1, \u03b1=0.99 per iteration.\n- Learning rate: 0.01, decaying by 0.1 every 1000 steps.\n- Variations: Start with random h or use higher starting resolution.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Coarse grids take O(1s) per iteration, finer grids up to O(10s).\n- Plan: 1000 iterations at 20 points, 500 each at 40 and 80, final polish at 200 points.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Final h must satisfy \u2211h = n_points / 2 and 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1.\n- Validate C\u2085 using original correlation method.\n- Check feasibility before returning.",
